    "body": "## What and why\n\nThe freshly hosted SpiralCore implementation supplies actual E8 operator routes. Record the source identity, two expert source reviews and bounded browser observations, and reconcile the Hamming/icosian basis boundaries with current native learning. Add a follow-up to the PDF assessment so its limits are not mistaken for absence of SpiralCore geometry.\n\n## Result\n\nKEEP finite action contracts as consolidation inputs; native model integration and language benefit NOT YET PROMOTED. Browser route0→86→1 takes2 operator hops with intrinsic length/trace4;0→4 is rejected across orbits. The256/256 fixture badge is explicitly application-reported. Half-integer sign-Hamming equality has its exact family/scale scope. The protected guard role adds no gradient credit; overlapping task/reference roles still contribute their declared weights; shared pooled-margin credit is the justified learner seam. No model/build/GPU work, accepted8/512 complete development replies unchanged.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Checks at exact head1dca333bdaea20992cd1374b0b4999b805cf186b: claim-wording gate PASS; diff check PASS. Rust/model tests not applicable to three Markdown files. Exact-head adversarial review PASS, review comment linked on PR.\n- [x] Research record: docs/labs/spiralcore-live-review-2026-10-09/README.md\n- [x] Newest current-state entry ends with Next\n- [x] SpiralCore documentation search inspected; historical v63/v68 scope remains accurate; current PDF record receives linked follow-up\n- [x] STATUS.md / ROADMAP.md / #2028 milestone table unchanged: no capability or accepted artifact change\n- [x] README unchanged: no implemented model mechanism, command or headline result changed\n- [x] python3 scripts/check_claim_wording.py PASS\n- [x] After merge: verify fresh main, delete branch/worktree, preserve results in iCloud, apply hygiene, report on milestone\n\nReferences #2030; follows #2085 and #2084.\n",
